    {
      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The amended text of 38 U.S.C. \u00a7 511(a), read with the constitutional-review provisions in 38 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 7261 and 7292, channels a constitutional question necessary to an individual veteran's benefits determination through the Board, Veterans Court, and Federal Circuit rather than a district court; Johnson v. Robison addressed materially different pre-VJRA text and a scheme lacking that judicial route."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The holding will categorically cover facial and as-applied attacks on a veterans-benefits statute when resolving the constitutional question is necessary to determine an individual claimant's entitlement or benefit amount, while reserving wholly collateral structural challenges to the VA's authority."
    }
  ],
